CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constrained templated conversion operator: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^.*is unknown.*$
--
[temp.deduct]/5, [temp.deduct.conv], [temp.constr.decl]: a conversion-function
template whose associated constraints (requires-clause) are not satisfied by the
deduced arguments is removed from the candidate set.  Models libstdc++'s
__max_size_type / __max_diff_type constrained templated conversion operators;
without the constraint check the front end instantiated a bogus "operator
<class>" and reported it unknown.
